kosha rubber

  -- natural rubber: polyisoprene (C5H8)n. latex from Hevea brasiliensis.
  -- synthetic rubber: styrene-butadiene (SBR), neoprene, silicone.
  -- an elastic polymer: long cross-linked chains stretch and return.
  -- vulcanisation (Goodyear 1844): sulfur cross-links between chains.
  --   cross-linking increases elasticity, strength, temperature resistance.
  -- without vulcanisation: sticky in heat, brittle in cold.
  --
  -- properties:
  --   elastic (e ≈ 0.75-0.85 depending on compound)
  --   electrical insulator (no free electrons)
  --   water resistant (non-polar chains repel water)
  --   low thermal conductivity (polymer — insulator)
  --   damping: absorbs vibration (used in mounts, tyres)
  --   coefficient of friction: high (grip)

